      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T16:46:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The interrupt was suspended before, calling the interrupt handler (`extpower_interrupt()`) here is like a new incoming interrupt. As the `extpower_interrupt()` has debouncing logic so it doesn\u0027t send the host event (`extpower_handle_update()`) if the GPIO level has no change. So you don\u0027t need to cache the previous GPIO level and check any change here.\n\nCalling `extpower_handler_update()` directly bypasses the internal state tracking, which could lead to desynchronization, e.g. the internal debounce state.",
      "parentUuid": "9c1ede78_83dcef64",
